      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1970s civic vision reshaped False Creek into a sustainability‑focused waterfront, leading to green spaces and people‑first design.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://beautifulbritishcolumbia.net/2025/07/22/false-creek-vancouver-from-industrial-past-to-sustainable-waterfront-living/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Southeast False Creek became the 2010 Winter Olympics Village, now a model green neighbourhood powered by renewable energy and rainwater harvesting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://beautifulbritishcolumbia.net/2025/07/22/false-creek-vancouver-from-industrial-past-to-sustainable-waterfront-living/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The creek’s eastern half was once a large tidal mudflat stretching from Cambie Street Bridge to Clark Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://falsecreekfriends.org/history",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "False Creek wraps around downtown Vancouver and borders neighbourhoods like Kitsilano and Mount Pleasant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://falsecreekfriends.org/history",
